//! The `page` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property is used to specify
//! the named page, a specific type of page defined by the `@page`
//! [at-rule](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Syntax/At-rules).
//!
//! Initial: auto. Inherited: no.
//! Percentages: not accepted.
//!
//! Keyword effects:
//! - auto: Default value. Use the value of the nearest ancestor with a non-`auto` value. If no
//! ancestor has a named page value set, the used value for auto is the empty string.
//!
//! Grammar: auto | <custom-ident>
